      "created_at": "2015-03-24T02:59:30.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Silverleaf\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/silverleaf/48/2332_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Silverleaf:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>If you use Haka to kill something that only has HP because of Imbued Vitality, does that work?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p><br><br>Imbued Viatality has always confused me to an extent- do cards with HP that don't normally have it lose their HP when Imbued Vitality goes away? If so, are they destroyed because they had HP and it's now dropped to zero?</p>",
