    {
      "id": 137839,
      "name": "Silverleaf",
      "username": "Silverleaf",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/silverleaf/{size}/2332_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-03-24T00:39:08.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"MarioFanaticXV\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mariofanaticxv/48/2129_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> MarioFanaticXV:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p><b>Silverleaf wrote:</b></p>\n<div><blockquote>If you use Haka to kill something that only has HP because of Imbued Vitality, does that work?</blockquote></div>\nImbued Viatality has always confused me to an extent- do cards with HP that don't normally have it lose their HP when Imbued Vitality goes away? If so, are they destroyed because they had HP and it's now dropped to zero? \n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I believe they lose their HP and are no longer a target. They don't have 0 HP, they just don't have any HP anymore so they aren't auto-destroyed.</p>\n<p>While Imbued Vitality is in play though, they have HP and can be destroyed by taking damage that drops them to 0 or below (or by Sucker Punch/Wrathful Gaze or similar).</p>",
      "post_number": 2,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:14:16.709Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
