      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "[quote=\"MarioFanaticXV\"]\n\n<b>Silverleaf wrote:</b>\n<div class=\"bb-quote\"><blockquote class=\"bb-quote-body\">If you use Haka to kill something that only has HP because of Imbued Vitality, does that work?</blockquote></div>\nImbued Viatality has always confused me to an extent- do cards with HP that don&#39;t normally have it lose their HP when Imbued Vitality goes away? If so, are they destroyed because they had HP and it&#39;s now dropped to zero? \n[/quote]\n \n\n I believe they lose their HP and are no longer a target. They don&#39;t have 0 HP, they just don&#39;t have any HP anymore so they aren&#39;t auto-destroyed. \n\nWhile Imbued Vitality is in play though, they have HP and can be destroyed by taking damage that drops them to 0 or below (or by Sucker Punch/Wrathful Gaze or similar).\n",
