    {
      "id": 137840,
      "name": "Matchstickman",
      "username": "Matchstickman",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/matchstickman/{size}/1880_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-03-24T00:41:54.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>When Imbued Vitality leaves play it doesn't drop HP to zero, it's just like a character card without a printed value (i.e. the incap sides of Hero cards or Miss Information), they don't have 0 HP they have no HP, they are not a target and are not destroyed because only targets with 0 (or less) HP are subject to destruction due to that.</p>",
      "post_number": 3,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:14:16.781Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.0,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 12721,
      "topic_slug": "imbued-vitality-question",
      "display_username": "Matchstickman",
      "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
      "flair_name": "playtesters",
